WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.438
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:01.438 --> 00:00:03.730
YAEL GRUSHKA-COCKAYNE: In
today's business environment,

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:06.740
data is a necessity.

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:10.760
This course will give you an
understanding of data science.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:14.330
So you think beyond just
spreadsheets and tables.

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:17.890
We will use real world
case studies to help

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:23.830
you understand common methodologies and
statistics, data analytics, and data

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:26.830
science along with some
basic skills on how

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:29.900
to apply them to your everyday work.

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:33.160
SUSANNA GALLANI: The role of
statistical analysis and data analytics

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:36.610
is to provide you with
conversation starters.

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:40.990
YAEL GRUSHKA-COCKAYNE: We will dive
into data wrangling, visualization,

00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:44.210
forecasting, and even machine learning.

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:46.960
You will learn how to
design visual models,

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:51.520
develop hypotheses, and draw insights
into actionable recommendations

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:53.050
for your business.

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:55.930
PAUL MATHERNE: What you need
to know as a data science

00:00:55.930 --> 00:01:01.405
analyst is that you have to always
be ready to change your model.

00:01:01.405 --> 00:01:04.030
YAEL GRUSHKA-COCKAYNE: This will
be taught through case studies

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:10.030
from retail, health care, financial
institutions, and even Hollywood.

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:12.280
TEMPLE FENNEL: I really
wanted to understand the data,

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:14.480
because producing a film can be costly.

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:17.065
But even more costly sometimes
can be the actual advertising.

00:01:17.065 --> 00:01:18.940
YAEL GRUSHKA-COCKAYNE:
Not only will you gain

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:22.360
the awareness of the technical
elements of data analysis,

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:25.630
this course will give you the
tools and the methodologies

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:27.293
to act upon the results.

00:01:27.293 --> 00:01:29.710
SUSANNA GALLANI: You can
actually maximize the performance

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:31.310
at the individual level.

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:35.067
And in aggregate, you will get a
better performance for the company.

00:01:35.067 --> 00:01:37.900
YAEL GRUSHKA-COCKAYNE: Can you
predict the future for your business?

